<title>BRAZIL: NatSteel,Gerdau new partners in Acominas.</title>
<headline>NatSteel,Gerdau new partners in Acominas.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Gerdau group and Singapore's NatSteel Ltd have become new partners in Brazilian steelmaker Acominas, financial daily Gazeta Mercantil said.</p>
<p>The paper said each has subscribed for 1,000 shares in Acominas and will make up part of a controlling consortium which also will include Japan's Marubeni Corp and a Malaysian trading firm.</p>
<p>The paper, which did not cite a source, said Acominas shareholders are expected to approve the moves at a June 27 meeting, when the consortium will secure its position with a payment of $150 million.</p>
<p>The consortium will buy shares and future debentures convertible to common shares through a capital increase totalling 214.7 million reais ($199.7 million), it said.</p>
<p>((--James Craig, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485413))</p>
